															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jim-north" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2191727); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2191727&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380259" alt="Jim North" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2191727)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jim-north" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2191727); return false;" >Jim North</a></span> <span class="odate time_1525270163 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 May 2018 14:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3787555">
									

<p>Don't take my snark away! It's the only thing I have going for me!</p>
<p>Funny thing is, originally there wasn't going to be a twist!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Spoilerish&nbsp;Rambling?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Spoilerish&nbsp;Rambling.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>In the beginning, I just wanted to do something simple, a spooky exploration log where a hapless D-Class gets et by a scary monster. It was right about the time said scary monster showed up that I completely lost interest in writing the article, and it took me almost two full days to figure out why. First off, it was boring me. There's no lack of stories here about just that sort of thing, and even though it was what I'd wanted to write, I realized it wasn't what I <em>really</em> wanted to write.</p>
<p>That leads to the second issue I had, which was that kind of story just not really being <em>me</em>. Bad guy wins, everybody gets spooped &#8230; I enjou reading that, sure, that's why I'm here, but it's not really my style of writing. When I decided hell with it, the D-Class ain't just gonna survive, she's gonna kick some gatdamned ass, the whole rest of the article just flowed out.</p>
<p>And yeah, the story then became less about the spooks and more about the Foundation and D-Class themselves, which I do feel works much better and is more interesting than the umpteenth guy getting his kidneys sliced into a pie.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anywho, glad ya liked it!</p>

